---
import Glow from '../components/Glow.astro'
import Frame from '../layouts/Frame.astro'

const repo = 'https://github.com/toni-bobocel/weft'

const chapters = [
  {
    mark: 'Clock',
    lines: ['Keeping order', 'without a', 'shared clock.'],
    rows: [
      ['Clock', 'Hybrid logical'],
      ['Ties', 'Broken by device id'],
      ['Stamps', 'Sort as plain text'],
      ['Too far ahead', 'Turned away after 60 s'],
    ],
    prose:
      "Devices disagree about the time, sometimes by minutes. So every edit is stamped by a hybrid logical clock: real time when machines agree, a small counter when they don't. If one edit happened before another, its stamp is always smaller, <em>whatever the wall clocks say</em>. The stamps still read like times, which helps a lot when you're debugging late.",
  },
  {
    mark: 'Text',
    lines: ['Text that', 'merges one', 'letter at a time.'],
    rows: [
      ['Structure', 'RGA sequence'],
      ['Each letter', 'Knows what it follows'],
      ['Same spot', 'Newest first'],
      ['Deleted letters', 'Kept, invisible'],
    ],
    prose:
      "Each character remembers the one it was typed after. When two people type in the same spot, <em>their words land whole, side by side</em>, instead of mixing letter by letter. If you type inside a word someone else just deleted, your letters stay: they're still hooked onto the deleted ones underneath.",
  },
  {
    mark: 'Sync',
    lines: ['Only send', 'what the other', 'side is missing.'],
    rows: [
      ['Each edit', 'Numbered per device'],
      ['Messages', 'Two kinds'],
      ['Arrives twice', 'Ignored'],
      ['Arrives early', 'Waits its turn'],
    ],
    prose:
      'Every edit gets a number per device. Swapping those numbers tells each side exactly what the other lacks, so coming back after a week offline <em>sends the week, not the database</em>. The server is just another copy that happens never to edit anything.',
  },
  {
    mark: 'Tests',
    lines: ["I don't trust it,", 'so I test it', 'a lot.'],
    rows: [
      ['Tool', 'fast-check'],
      ['Histories', '1,500 locally, 15,000 in CI'],
      ['What goes wrong', 'Loss, repeats, reordering, bad clocks'],
      ['Pass means', 'Every copy identical'],
    ],
    prose:
      "A property test writes thousands of random histories: people editing at the same time, clocks jumping backwards, a network that loses and repeats things. At the end every copy has to match, byte for byte. On its second run it caught a real bug: <em>just reading a note created an empty one</em>. A bit embarrassing, and exactly why the test is there.",
  },
]

const records = [
  ['Why I wrote the CRDTs instead of using Yjs or Automerge', '0001-own-the-crdt.md'],
  ['Why every timestamp comes from a hybrid clock', '0002-hybrid-logical-clocks.md'],
  ['Why text is an RGA, and why deleted letters stay', '0003-rga-for-text.md'],
  ['Why sync is a log of edits and the server is just a copy', '0004-op-log-and-version-vectors.md'],
]

const stack = [
  ['TypeScript', 'everywhere'],
  ['No dependencies', 'in the engine'],
  ['node:sqlite', 'the relay keeps its log here'],
  ['ws', 'for the relay'],
  ['fast-check', 'for the tests'],
  ['Vitest', 'runs them'],
  ['three.js', 'the cloud and the water'],
  ['GSAP', 'everything that moves'],
]
---

<Frame title="Weft, how it works" page="engine">
  <p class="ident">engine<span>how it holds together</span></p>

  <div class="section-mark mono" aria-hidden="true">
    <i><b data-progress></b></i>
    <span data-mark>Clock</span>
  </div>

  <article class="read">
    {
      chapters.map((c) => (
        <section class="chapter" data-chapter={c.mark}>
          <Glow lines={c.lines} />
          <table class="kv mono">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Key</th>
                <th>Value</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {c.rows.map(([k, v]) => (
                <tr>
                  <th>{k}</th>
                  <td>{v}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="prose" set:html={c.prose} />
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <section class="chapter" data-chapter="Choices">
      <Glow lines={["Why it's", 'built', 'this way.']} />
      <ul class="records">
        {
          records.map(([title, file]) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/adr/${file}`}>
                <b>{title}</b>
                <span class="mono dim">↗</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" data-chapter="Stack">
      <Glow lines={['Not much', 'underneath,', 'on purpose.']} />
      <div class="ghosts">
        {
          stack.map(([name, role]) => (
            <div>
              <b>{name}</b>
              <span class="mono dim">{role}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Frame>
